ompetitions/playground-series-s4e1) and place it in the same folder as this notebook.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 2. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) <a id='2'></a>","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- General overview ---\nprint('=== TRAIN DATASET ===' if 'df_train' in dir() else '=== TEST DATASET (no train loaded) ===')\ndf = df_train if 'df_train' in dir() else df_test\n\nprint(f'Shape: {df.shape}')\nprint(f'\\nColumn types:')\nprint(df.dtypes)\nprint(f'\\nMissing values:')\nprint(df.isnull().sum())","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"df.describe()","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Target distribution (class balance) ---\n# Run only if train.csv is loaded\nif 'df_train' in dir() and 'y' in df_train.columns:\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(10, 4))\n\n    # Count plot\n    counts = df_train['y'].value_counts()\n    axes[0].bar(['No (0)', 'Yes (1)'], counts.values, color=['steelblue', 'coral'])\n    axes[0].set_title('Target class distribution')\n    axes[0].set_ylabel('Count')\n    for i, v in enumerate(counts.values):\n        axes[0].text(i, v + 100, f'{v:,} ({v/len(df_train)*100:.1f}%)', ha='center')\n\n    # Pie chart\n    axes[1].pie(counts.values, labels=['No (0)', 'Yes (1)'],\n                autopct='%1.1f%%', colors=['steelblue', 'coral'], startangle=90)\n    axes[1].set_title('Class balance')\n\n    plt.suptitle('Target variable: term deposit subscription', fontsize=13, y=1.02)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()\n\n    imbalance_ratio = counts[0] / counts[1]\n    print(f'Class imbalance ratio: {imbalance_ratio:.1f}:1 (No:Yes)')\n    print('→ We must use class_weight=\"balanced\" or AUC-ROC metric, NOT accuracy.')\nelse:\n    print('Load train.csv to see the target distribution.')","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Numerical features distributions ---\nnum_cols = ['age', 'balance', 'duration', 'campaign', 'pdays', 'previous']\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(15, 8))\naxes = axes.flatten()\n\nfor i, col in enumerate(num_cols):\n    data = df_train[col] if 'df_train' in dir() else df_test[col]\n    axes[i].hist(data, bins=50, color='steelblue', alpha=0.7, edgecolor='white')\n    axes[i].set_title(f'{col}')\n    axes[i].set_xlabel('Value')\n    axes[i].set_ylabel('Count')\n    # Add median line\n    axes[i].axvline(data.median(), color='coral', linestyle='--', label=f'Median: {data.median():.0f}')\n    axes[i].legend(fontsize=9)\n\nplt.suptitle('Distribution of numerical features', fontsize=14)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\nprint('Note: balance can be negative (overdrafts). pdays=-1 means client was not contacted before.')","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Categorical features ---\ncat_cols = ['job', 'marital', 'education', 'default', 'housing', 'loan', 'contact', 'month', 'poutcome']\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 3, figsize=(16, 12))\naxes = axes.flatten()\n\ndf_plot = df_train if 'df_train' in dir() else df_test\n\nfor i, col in enumerate(cat_cols):\n    vc = df_plot[col].value_counts()\n    axes[i].barh(vc.index, vc.values, color='steelblue', alpha=0.8)\n    axes[i].set_title(col)\n    axes[i].set_xlabel('Count')\n\nplt.suptitle('Categorical features — value counts', fontsize=14)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Target vs key features (only if train is loaded) ---\nif 'df_train' in dir() and 'y' in df_train.columns:\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(16, 5))\n\n    # Duration vs target\n    for label, color in [(0, 'steelblue'), (1, 'coral')]:\n        axes[0].hist(df_train[df_train['y'] == label]['duration'],\n                     bins=50, alpha=0.6, color=color, label=f'y={label}')\n    axes[0].set_title('Call duration by target')\n    axes[0].set_xlabel('duration (seconds)')\n    axes[0].legend()\n\n    # Job vs subscription rate\n    job_rate = df_train.groupby('job')['y'].mean().sort_values(ascending=True)\n    axes[1].barh(job_rate.index, job_rate.values, color='mediumseagreen', alpha=0.8)\n    axes[1].set_title('Subscription rate by job')\n    axes[1].set_xlabel('Subscription rate')\n    axes[1].axvline(df_train['y'].mean(), color='coral', linestyle='--', label='Overall mean')\n    axes[1].legend()\n\n    # Month vs subscription rate\n    month_order = ['jan','feb','mar','apr','may','jun','jul','aug','sep','oct','nov','dec']\n    month_rate = df_train.groupby('month')['y'].mean().reindex(\n        [m for m in month_order if m in df_train['month'].unique()])\n    axes[2].bar(month_rate.index, month_rate.values, color='mediumpurple', alpha=0.8)\n    axes[2].set_title('Subscription rate by month')\n    axes[2].set_xlabel('month')\n    axes[2].set_ylabel('rate')\n\n    plt.suptitle('Key feature analysis vs target', fontsize=13)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()\nelse:\n    print('Load train.csv for target analysis plots.')","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Correlation matrix (numerical features only) ---\ndf_plot = df_train if 'df_train' in dir() else df_test\nnum_df = df_plot[num_cols]\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 6))\ncorr = num_df.corr()\nmask = np.triu(np.ones_like(corr, dtype=bool))\nsns.heatmap(corr, mask=mask, annot=True, fmt='.2f', cmap='coolwarm',\n            center=0, square=True, ax=ax)\nax.set_title('Correlation matrix — numerical features')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**EDA Observations:**\n- `duration` (call duration) is the most informative single feature — longer calls → higher subscription rate\n- Strong class imbalance (~88% No, ~12% Yes) → use AUC-ROC, not accuracy\n- `pdays = -1` encodes 'never contacted' → we'll create a binary flag\n- `unknown` appears in multiple categorical columns — treat as a valid category\n- No missing values in this dataset","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 3. Preprocessing & Feature Engineering <a id='3'></a>","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def preprocess(df, is_train=True):\n    \"\"\"Apply feature engineering and return X (and y if train).\"\"\"\n    df = df.copy()\n\n    # --- Feature engineering ---\n\n    # 1. Binary flag: was the client contacted in a previous campaign?\n    df['was_contacted_before'] = (df['pdays'] != -1).astype(int)\n\n    # 2. Replace pdays=-1 with 0 (no previous contact = 0 days ago is misleading;\n    #    we keep the flag above and set a neutral value)\n    df['pdays'] = df['pdays'].replace(-1, 0)\n\n    # 3. Month as integer (cyclical order matters)\n    month_map = {'jan':1,'feb':2,'mar':3,'apr':4,'may':5,'jun':6,\n                 'jul':7,'aug':8,'sep':9,'oct':10,'nov':11,'dec':12}\n    df['month_num'] = df['month'].map(month_map)\n\n    # 4. Balance sign flag\n    df['negative_balance'] = (df['balance'] < 0).astype(int)\n\n    # Define feature columns\n    NUMERICAL = ['age', 'balance', 'duration', 'campaign',\n                 'pdays', 'previous', 'month_num',\n                 'was_contacted_before', 'negative_balance']\n\n    CATEGORICAL = ['job', 'marital', 'education', 'default',\n                   'housing', 'loan', 'contact', 'poutcome']\n\n    X = df[NUMERICAL + CATEGORICAL]\n\n    if is_train and 'y' in df.columns:\n        y = df['y']\n        return X, y, NUMERICAL, CATEGORICAL\n    return X, NUMERICAL, CATEGORICAL\n\n\n# Build preprocessor (ColumnTransformer)\ndef build_preprocessor(numerical_cols, categorical_cols):\n    from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OrdinalEncoder\n    from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n\n    return ColumnTransformer(transformers=[\n        ('num', StandardScaler(), numerical_cols),\n        ('cat', OrdinalEncoder(handle_unknown='use_encoded_value', unknown_value=-1), categorical_cols)\n    ], remainder='drop')\n\n\n# Apply preprocessing\nif 'df_train' in dir() and 'y' in df_train.columns:\n    X, y, NUM_COLS, CAT_COLS = preprocess(df_train, is_train=True)\n    print(f'X shape: {X.shape} | y shape: {y.shape}')\n    print(f'Positive class rate: {y.mean():.3f}')\n    X.head(3)\nelse:\n    print('Load train.csv to build X and y.')","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 4. Modeling — 3 Classifiers <a id='4'></a>\n\nWe train three classifiers:\n1. **Logistic Regression** — linear baseline, highly interpretable\n2. **Random Forest** — non-linear ensemble, robust to outliers\n3. **XGBoost** — gradient boosting, usually best performance on tabular data","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"if 'X' not in dir():\n    print('Run the preprocessing cell first (load train.csv).')\nelse:\n    preprocessor = build_preprocessor(NUM_COLS, CAT_COLS)\n\n    # --- Model 1: Logistic Regression ---\n    model_lr = Pipeline([\n        ('pre', preprocessor),\n        ('clf', LogisticRegression(\n            class_weight='balanced',\n            max_iter=1000,\n            random_state=SEED\n        ))\n    ])\n\n    # --- Model 2: Random Forest ---\n    model_rf = Pipeline([\n        ('pre', build_preprocessor(NUM_COLS, CAT_COLS)),\n        ('clf', RandomForestClassifier(\n            n_estimators=200,\n            class_weight='balanced',\n            max_depth=10,\n            n_jobs=-1,\n            random_state=SEED\n        ))\n    ])\n\n    # --- Model 3: XGBoost (or GBM fallback) ---\n    if USE_XGB:\n        # Compute scale_pos_weight to handle imbalance\n        neg, pos = (y == 0).sum(), (y == 1).sum()\n        spw = neg / pos\n        model_boost = Pipeline([\n            ('pre', build_preprocessor(NUM_COLS, CAT_COLS)),\n            ('clf', XGBClassifier(\n                n_estimators=300,\n                learning_rate=0.05,\n                max_depth=6,\n                scale_pos_weight=spw,\n                eval_metric='auc',\n                random_state=SEED,\n                n_jobs=-1\n            ))\n        ])\n    else:\n        model_boost = Pipeline([\n            ('pre', build_preprocessor(NUM_COLS, CAT_COLS)),\n            ('clf', GradientBoostingClassifier(\n                n_estimators=200,\n                learning_rate=0.05,\n                max_depth=5,\n                random_state=SEED\n            ))\n        ])\n\n    models = {\n        'Logistic Regression': model_lr,\n        'Random Forest':       model_rf,\n        'XGBoost' if USE_XGB else 'GBM': model_boost\n    }\n\n    print('Models defined:')\n    for name, m in models.items():\n        print(f'  • {name}: {m[\"clf\"].__class__.__name__}')","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 5. Cross-Validation & Metrics Comparison <a id='5'></a>","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"if 'X' not in dir():\n    print('Load train.csv first.')\nelse:\n    from sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold, cross_validate\n\n    cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=SEED)\n    scoring = ['roc_auc', 'f1', 'precision', 'recall']\n\n    results = {}\n    for name, model in models.items():\n        print(f'Training {name}...', end=' ')\n        cv_res = cross_validate(model, X, y, cv=cv, scoring=scoring,\n                                n_jobs=-1, return_train_score=False)\n        results[name] = cv_res\n        auc = cv_res['test_roc_auc'].mean()\n        f1  = cv_res['test_f1'].mean()\n        print(f'AUC = {auc:.4f} | F1 = {f1:.4f}')\n\n    print('\\nDone!')","metadata":{"scrolled":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"if 'results' in dir():\n    # --- Build comparison table ---\n    summary = []\n    for name, res in results.items():\n        summary.append({\n            'Model': name,\n            'AUC-ROC (mean)': res['test_roc_auc'].mean(),\n            'AUC-ROC (std)':  res['test_roc_auc'].std(),\n            'F1 (mean)':      res['test_f1'].mean(),\n            'Precision':      res['test_precision'].mean(),\n            'Recall':         res['test_recall'].mean(),\n        })\n    df_results = pd.DataFrame(summary).set_index('Model')\n    df_results = df_results.sort_values('AUC-ROC (mean)', ascending=False)\n\n    print('=== 5-Fold Cross-Validation Results ===')\n    print(df_results.round(4).to_string())\n\n    # --- Visual comparison ---\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n\n    # Box plots AUC\n    auc_data = {name: res['test_roc_auc'] for name, res in results.items()}\n    axes[0].boxplot(auc_data.values(), labels=auc_data.keys(), patch_artist=True,\n                    boxprops=dict(facecolor='steelblue', alpha=0.5))\n    axes[0].set_title('AUC-ROC across 5 folds')\n    axes[0].set_ylabel('AUC-ROC')\n    axes[0].tick_params(axis='x', rotation=15)\n\n    # Bar chart F1\n    f1_means = {name: res['test_f1'].mean() for name, res in results.items()}\n    f1_stds  = {name: res['test_f1'].std()  for name, res in results.items()}\n    axes[1].bar(f1_means.keys(), f1_means.values(),\n                yerr=f1_stds.values(), capsize=5,\n                color=['steelblue','mediumseagreen','coral'], alpha=0.8)\n    axes[1].set_title('F1-score comparison (mean ± std)')\n    axes[1].set_ylabel('F1-score')\n    axes[1].tick_params(axis='x', rotation=15)\n\n    plt.suptitle('Model comparison — 5-fold cross-validation', fontsize=13)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- ROC curves on a held-out validation split ---\nif 'X' in dir():\n    from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n\n    X_tr, X_val, y_tr, y_val = train_test_split(\n        X, y, test_size=0.2, stratify=y, random_state=SEED)\n\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 6))\n\n    colors = ['steelblue', 'mediumseagreen', 'coral']\n    for (name, model), color in zip(models.items(), colors):\n        model.fit(X_tr, y_tr)\n        RocCurveDisplay.from_estimator(model, X_val, y_val, ax=ax,\n                                       name=name, color=color)\n\n    ax.plot([0, 1], [0, 1], 'k--', label='Random classifier')\n    ax.set_title('ROC Curves — Validation set (20%)')\n    ax.legend(loc='lower right')\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Confusion matrices ---\nif 'X_val' in dir():\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, len(models), figsize=(5 * len(models), 4))\n    if len(models) == 1:\n        axes = [axes]\n\n    for ax, (name, model) in zip(axes, models.items()):\n        ConfusionMatrixDisplay.from_estimator(\n            model, X_val, y_val,\n            display_labels=['No (0)', 'Yes (1)'],\n            cmap='Blues', ax=ax, colorbar=False\n        )\n        ax.set_title(name)\n\n    plt.suptitle('Confusion matrices — Validation set', fontsize=13)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 6. Hyperparameter Optimization <a id='6'></a>\n\nWe optimize the best performing model using `RandomizedSearchCV`.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import pandas as pd\nfrom scipy.stats import randint\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import RandomizedSearchCV, StratifiedKFold\n\nSEED = 42\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Vérification des données\n# -----------------------------\nif 'X' not in dir() or 'y' not in dir():\n    print('Load train.csv first.')\nelse:\n\n    # -----------------------------\n    # Échantillonnage (accélération)\n    # -----------------------------\n    USE_SAMPLE = True  # True = utilise 30% des données pour accélérer fortement\n\n    if USE_SAMPLE:\n        # Réduction du dataset → gain de temps majeur (souvent x3 à x5)\n        X_train = X.sample(frac=0.3, random_state=SEED)\n        y_train = y.loc[X_train.index]\n    else:\n        X_train, y_train = X, y\n\n    # -----------------------------\n    # Pipeline\n    # -----------------------------\n    rf_pipeline = Pipeline([\n        ('pre', build_preprocessor(NUM_COLS, CAT_COLS)),  # preprocessing refait à chaque fold\n        ('clf', RandomForestClassifier(\n            class_weight='balanced',\n            random_state=SEED,\n            n_jobs=-1  # utilise tous les CPU\n        ))\n    ])\n\n    # -----------------------------\n    # Espace de recherche réduit\n    # -----------------------------\n    rf_param_dist = {\n        # Réduit de [100–500] → [50–200]\n        # Moins d’arbres = gain direct de temps\n        'clf__n_estimators': randint(50, 200),\n\n        # Réduit de [5–20] → [5–15]\n        # Moins profond = arbres plus rapides à construire\n        'clf__max_depth': randint(5, 15),\n\n        # Réduit de [2–20] → [2–10]\n        # Moins de combinaisons inutiles\n        'clf__min_samples_split': randint(2, 10),\n\n        # Réduit de [1–10] → [1–5]\n        # Simplification du search space\n        'clf__min_samples_leaf': randint(1, 5),\n\n        # Supprime 0.5 pour réduire les possibilités\n        'clf__max_features': ['sqrt', 'log2']\n    }\n\n    # -----------------------------\n    # Validation croisée\n    # -----------------------------\n    cv = StratifiedKFold(\n        n_splits=3,  # réduit de 5 → 3 (≈ 40% plus rapide)\n        shuffle=True,\n        random_state=SEED\n    )\n\n    # -----------------------------\n    # Randomized Search\n    # -----------------------------\n    rf_search = RandomizedSearchCV(\n        estimator=rf_pipeline,\n        param_distributions=rf_param_dist,\n        \n        n_iter=10,  # réduit de 20 → 10 (divise le nombre de modèles testés par 2)\n        \n        scoring='roc_auc',\n        cv=cv,\n        verbose=2,\n        random_state=SEED,\n        n_jobs=-1  # parallélisation maximale\n    )\n\n    # -----------------------------\n    # Entraînement\n    # -----------------------------\n    print('Running RandomizedSearchCV (fast mode)...')\n    rf_search.fit(X_train, y_train)\n\n    # -----------------------------\n    # Résultats\n    # -----------------------------\n    print('\\nBest AUC-ROC:', round(rf_search.best_score_, 4))\n\n    print('\\nBest parameters:')\n    for k, v in rf_search.best_params_.items():\n        print(f'{k}: {v}')\n\n    # -----------------------------\n    # Modèle final\n    # -----------------------------\n    best_model = rf_search.best_estimator_\n\n    # Réentraînement sur toutes les données\n    # Important : compense l'utilisation du sample\n    print('\\nRetraining best model on full dataset...')\n    best_model.fit(X, y)\n\n    print('Model ready.')","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Optimize XGBoost (if available) ---\nif USE_XGB and 'X' in dir():\n    from scipy.stats import randint, uniform\n\n    neg, pos = (y == 0).sum(), (y == 1).sum()\n    spw = neg / pos\n\n    xgb_pipeline = Pipeline([\n        ('pre', build_preprocessor(NUM_COLS, CAT_COLS)),\n        ('clf', XGBClassifier(\n            scale_pos_weight=spw, eval_metric='auc',\n            random_state=SEED, n_jobs=-1))\n    ])\n\n    xgb_param_dist = {\n        'clf__n_estimators':  randint(100, 500),\n        'clf__learning_rate': uniform(0.01, 0.2),\n        'clf__max_depth':     randint(3, 10),\n        'clf__subsample':     uniform(0.6, 0.4),\n        'clf__colsample_bytree': uniform(0.5, 0.5),\n        'clf__gamma':         uniform(0, 5),\n    }\n\n    xgb_search = RandomizedSearchCV(\n        xgb_pipeline, xgb_param_dist,\n        n_iter=20, scoring='roc_auc',\n        cv=StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=SEED),\n        random_state=SEED, n_jobs=-1, verbose=1\n    )\n\n    print('Running RandomizedSearchCV on XGBoost (20 iterations)...')\n    xgb_search.fit(X, y)\n\n    print(f'\\nBest XGBoost AUC-ROC: {xgb_search.best_score_:.4f}')\n    print(f'Best parameters:')\n    for k, v in xgb_search.best_params_.items():\n        print(f'  {k}: {v}')\n\n    best_model = xgb_search.best_estimator_\nelse:\n    if 'rf_search' in dir():\n        best_model = rf_search.best_estimator_\n        print('Using best Random Forest as final model.')","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 7. Interpretation & Feature Importance <a id='7'></a>","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Feature importance from Random Forest ---\nif 'X' in dir():\n    # Fit a fresh RF on all data for feature importance\n    rf_for_importance = Pipeline([\n        ('pre', build_preprocessor(NUM_COLS, CAT_COLS)),\n        ('clf', RandomForestClassifier(\n            n_estimators=300, class_weight='balanced',\n            max_depth=10, n_jobs=-1, random_state=SEED))\n    ])\n    rf_for_importance.fit(X, y)\n\n    feature_names = NUM_COLS + CAT_COLS\n    importances = rf_for_importance.named_steps['clf'].feature_importances_\n    fi_df = pd.DataFrame({'feature': feature_names, 'importance': importances})\n    fi_df = fi_df.sort_values('importance', ascending=True)\n\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 7))\n    colors_fi = ['steelblue' if i < len(NUM_COLS) else 'coral'\n                 for i in fi_df.index]\n    ax.barh(fi_df['feature'], fi_df['importance'], color=colors_fi, alpha=0.85)\n    ax.set_title('Feature Importance — Random Forest', fontsize=13)\n    ax.set_xlabel('Importance (mean decrease in impurity)')\n\n    from matplotlib.patches import Patch\n    legend_elements = [\n        Patch(facecolor='steelblue', alpha=0.85, label='Numerical'),\n        Patch(facecolor='coral',     alpha=0.85, label='Categorical')\n    ]\n    ax.legend(handles=legend_elements, loc='lower right')\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()\n    print('Top 3 features:', fi_df.nlargest(3, 'importance')['feature'].tolist())","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Logistic Regression coefficients ---\nif 'X' in dir():\n    lr_for_coef = Pipeline([\n        ('pre', build_preprocessor(NUM_COLS, CAT_COLS)),\n        ('clf', LogisticRegression(class_weight='balanced', max_iter=1000, random_state=SEED))\n    ])\n    lr_for_coef.fit(X, y)\n\n    coefs = lr_for_coef.named_steps['clf'].coef_[0]\n    coef_df = pd.DataFrame({'feature': NUM_COLS + CAT_COLS, 'coefficient': coefs})\n    coef_df = coef_df.sort_values('coefficient', ascending=True)\n\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 7))\n    colors_coef = ['coral' if c > 0 else 'steelblue' for c in coef_df['coefficient']]\n    ax.barh(coef_df['feature'], coef_df['coefficient'], color=colors_coef, alpha=0.85)\n    ax.axvline(0, color='black', linewidth=0.8)\n    ax.set_title('Logistic Regression coefficients', fontsize=13)\n    ax.set_xlabel('Coefficient value (positive → increases P(subscribe))')\n\n    from matplotlib.patches import Patch\n    legend_elements = [\n        Patch(facecolor='coral',     alpha=0.85, label='Positive effect'),\n        Patch(facecolor='steelblue', alpha=0.85, label='Negative effect')\n    ]\n    ax.legend(handles=legend_elements)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Classification report on validation set ---\nif 'X_val' in dir() and 'best_model' in dir():\n    print('=== Classification Report — Best model on validation set ===')\n    y_pred = best_model.predict(X_val)\n    print(classification_report(y_val, y_pred, target_names=['No (0)', 'Yes (1)']))","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Interpretation notes:**\n- `duration` is the strongest predictor — clients who talk longer are far more likely to subscribe\n- `poutcome = success` (previous campaign outcome) strongly increases subscription probability\n- `month` and `contact` type are informative — March, September, October, December show higher rates\n- **Limitation:** `duration` is only known *after* the call ends → in a real deployment, it cannot be used for prospecting\n- **Improvement directions:** Try SMOTE for class balancing, SHAP values for deeper explanations, feature selection","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 8. Final Predictions & Submission <a id='8'></a>","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Generate predictions for test set ---\nif 'best_model' in dir():\n    X_test, _, _ = preprocess(df_test, is_train=False)\n\n    # Retrain best model on full training data\n    best_model.fit(X, y)\n\n    # Predict probabilities (Kaggle expects probability of class 1)\n    y_test_proba = best_model.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n\n    # Build submission\n    submission = pd.DataFrame({'id': df_test['id'], 'y': y_test_proba})\n    submission.to_csv('submission.csv', index=False)\n\n    print(f'Submission saved: {submission.shape}')\n    print(f'Predicted probability range: [{y_test_proba.min():.3f}, {y_test_proba.max():.3f}]')\n    print(f'Mean predicted probability: {y_test_proba.mean():.3f}')\n    submission.head(10)\nelse:\n    print('Run the hyperparameter optimization cells first to define best_model.')","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# --- Distribution of predicted probabilities ---\nif 'y_test_proba' in dir():\n    plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n    plt.hist(y_test_proba, bins=50, color='steelblue', alpha=0.8, edgecolor='white')\n    plt.axvline(0.5, color='coral', linestyle='--', label='Threshold = 0.5')\n    plt.title('Distribution of predicted probabilities on test set')\n    plt.xlabel('P(subscribe = 1)')\n    plt.ylabel('Count')\n    plt.legend()\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## Summary\n\n| Step | Key choices made |\n|------|------------------|\n| EDA | Identified class imbalance (~88/12%), key features (duration, poutcome) |\n| Preprocessing | OrdinalEncoder for categoricals, StandardScaler for numericals, 4 engineered features |\n| Modeling | Logistic Regression (baseline), Random Forest, XGBoost |\n| Validation | StratifiedKFold (5 folds), AUC-ROC as primary metric |\n| Optimization | RandomizedSearchCV (20 iterations per model) |\n| Interpretation | Feature importance (RF), coefficients (LR), confusion matrices |\n| Limitations | `duration` leaks post-call info; class imbalance may cause false negatives |\n\n> **Note:** Kaggle score is not a grading criterion. Focus on understanding and justifying each choice.","metadata":{}}]}